Note that there can be only one special room per level, and that the
cockatrice nest is not one of the first checked for... As soon as there
is another one chosen, you cannot get a nest anymore.

So the chance isn't 1/8; it's much less. Suppose we're talking about
level 17, the first where a nest can appear.

Then we have:
  3/17 chance of a shop,
  1/6  chance of a throne room,
  1/8  chance of a leprechaun hall,
  1/7  chance of a zoo,
  1/5  chance of a temple,
  1/5  chance of a beehive,
  1/6  chance of a graveyard,
  1/8  chance of an anthole,
  1/4  chance of a barracks,
  1/6  chance of a swamp level, and FINALLY
  1/8  chance of a cockatrice nest.

So that should be a

   14 * 5 * 7 * 6 * 4 * 4 * 5 * 7 * 3 * 5     1      24.696.000
  ---------------------------------------- * --- = ---------------
   17 * 6 * 8 * 7 * 5 * 5 * 6 * 8 * 4 * 6     8     1.316.044.800

This amounts to a chance of only 1,88% on level 17.

Of course, the chance on level 18 is slightly greater, since 14/17
becomes 15/18 there (less chance of a shop). On level 19, the chance is
even greater, and so on. Below Medusa, no shops are generated so it
becomes 1/1.

Also, this supposes that leprechauns, killer bees, soldiers and
cockatrices have not been genocided and aren't extinct.

